From cde4fd9af01da8635f3750a90ccee2a9004b2f8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sixvolts <rigel@sixvolts.org>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:50:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: GCN repack for Q4_0 and the IQ4_NL / IQ4_XS / IQ3_S
 family, Q3_K relabelled to Q6_K planes, narrow MMQ tiles (crossport P2/R11,
 P5/R12)

Q4_0 (R11), end to end: host repack (nibble plane as on disk + fp16 d plane), decode matvec
(ROWS=2; the -8 offset taken in the integer domain against the quantized activation sum, which is
the exact integer the bytewise sub8 form computes), dense gate+up GLU, 2..16-column nc path, and
the MMQ tile (sub8 at LDS staging, one float scale). 2D weights only; GGML_CUDA_REPACK_Q4_0=0
opts out. test-repack-bench --check vs canonical: nmse 1.5e-4 (the offset method, by design).
Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_0 on one MI50: PPL equal to canonical, tg64 122.8 -> 143.6, pp2..16 +10..20%,
pp512 +2.4%. 5120x17408 matvec 129 -> 111 us; 5376x21504 163 -> 128.

IQ4_NL / IQ4_XS / IQ3_S (R12) relabel onto the same two planes: IQ4_NL exactly, IQ4_XS with
d*(ls-32) and IQ3_S with d*(1+2s) folded to one fp16 per sub-block (<= 4.5e-4 relative;
nmse vs canonical 3..9e-8), IQ3_S values stored as the nibble (v+15)/2. The kernels are the Q4_0
ones with a 16-entry codebook (two perm lookups per word) instead of q-8; one template parameter.
GGML_CUDA_REPACK_IQ=0 opts out. Qwen3.5-4B test quants: IQ3_S tg64 86 -> 124, pp512 1346 -> 1668;
IQ4_NL tg64 115 -> 119, pp512 1288 -> 1648; IQ4_XS tg64 114 -> 119, pp512 1413 -> 1646; PPL within
noise of canonical for all three. Per-matvec, canonical IQ4_XS decode (4.25 bpw, mmvq) is still
faster at one column on the largest shapes (100 vs 138 us at 5120x17408): the codebook decode is
ALU-bound; prefill and small batches are 30..50% faster.

Q3_K -> Q6_K relabel (exact: q6 = q3 + 28, the signed per-16 scales carry over): Q3_K weights
are repacked as Q6_K planes and run every Q6_K kernel, so they get the nc path and the fast
Q6_K tile. GGML_CUDA_Q3K_RELABEL=0 keeps the 3-bit kernels. Qwen3.5-4B-Q3_K_M: PPL bit-identical,
tg64 103 -> 107, pp3 45 -> 184, pp512 931 -> 1490. Matvec 204 -> 154 us, tile 34.4 -> 25.5 ms.

Dense prefill tiles pick the token tile width from the column count (16/32/48 for <= 48
columns, 64 above; GGML_CUDA_NO_MMQ_NARROW=1 restores 64): Q4_0 5120x17408 at 24 columns
843 -> 570 us.

tests/test-repack-host: CPU-only layout check of every repack format against ggml's reference
dequantizer (bit-exact for Q4_0, IQ4_NL, Q3_K, Q6_K; fp16-fold tolerance for IQ4_XS, IQ3_S).
test-repack-bench gains the nibble-format dense shapes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DTjwwGh3znQpq4Yoxunx6b
